    "question": "A patient returns from a camping trip, where he vacationed for several days in a tick-endemic environment. One month after his return home, he visited his healthcare provider with complaints of fatigue, numbness and history of rash surrounding an insect bite that occurred immediately on his return home from vacation. Suspecting Lyme disease, his clinician ordered an ELISA to test for Lyme antibody, results of which were equivocal on two different tests. His health care provider then ordered follow-up testing with:",
