    "question": "Hepatitis B, a disease arising from a DNA virus, is diagnosed in its acute phase via serology for HBsAg, HBcIgM and total alpha-HBc. Once a patient reaches chronic HBV infection, effectiveness of therapy may be evaluated using:",
